# Environment
.env
*.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Local databases
*.db
instance/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Agent worktrees: whole checkouts of this repo, which git would otherwise
# record as gitlinks to commits no clone can resolve.
.claude/worktrees/

# Scratch notes, not the repo.
drive/todo.txt

# Working pictures from `drive/tools/track_views.py` - a plan view and several
# from the road, taken while authoring a track and looked at once. The switcher's
# previews under drive/static/img/tracks/ ARE committed; these are not, because a
# five-view set per track per attempt would be tens of megabytes of pictures
# nobody reads twice.
drive/tools/views/

# Intermediate frames from `drive/tools/shoot_video.py`. The script renders each
# beat to a few hundred PNGs and ffmpeg stitches them into the mp4s beside them,
# then the next run clears and re-renders the lot - so these are build output,
# not source. Committed they would be 221MB of the repo forever, on top of the
# ~484MB of media already in .git that CI works around with sparse checkouts.
# The finished clips (drive/media/video/*.mp4 and beats/) ARE committed.
drive/media/video/frames/

# Storefront cover art from `drive/tools/shoot_covers.py` - the same hero shot
# every track already carries, at three portal sizes with the wordmark over it.
# A deliverable for somewhere else rather than something this site serves, and
# six files per track: `static/img/tracks/` is the committed set.
drive/covers/

# Contact sheets from the same script's `--probe`, used once to pick the start
# time of each beat by eye. Those times are now constants in the script, so the
# sheets are scouting output the same way drive/tools/views/ is.
drive/media/video/probe/

# GTO trainer: the opponent avatars are photographs of real people and this
# repo is public. They live outside the tree in prod (/home/ubuntu/gto-avatars,
# the same reasoning as accounts' AVATAR_DIR) and are served only to a logged-in
# owner, so a copy is never committed here either.
gto/avatars/

# The scratch track folder `tests/test_track_folders.py` writes. It only exists
# while that suite is running - the fixture removes it in a `finally` - and it
# is *deliberately* broken, because the file's whole subject is that a bad
# folder is contained rather than fatal. So a `git add -A` during a local run
# commits a track designed to fail `test_every_track_folder_loads`, which is
# precisely what it then does, in CI, blocking the deploy.
drive/tracks/zzscratch/
